WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.850
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.130
being released all the time,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.770
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.350
to test for ourselves.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.458
This is definitely one of those

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:12.420
TikTok-made-me-buy-it kind of products.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.003
This is the Pseudo Labs PHreckles Kit.

00:00:15.003 --> 00:00:16.569
It's nothing like any other

00:00:16.569 --> 00:00:18.980
faux-freckle product I've ever seen.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.110
You basically get the freckle liquid,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.970
which has a little round brush in it,

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.792
and this little toothpick-looking thing

00:00:24.792 --> 00:00:27.672
that you use to flick
the liquid onto your face

00:00:27.672 --> 00:00:30.040
to give you very natural-looking freckles.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.960
I knew this was going
to be a messy process,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.640
so I tucked a paper towel in my shirt

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.899
and just went at it.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.538
Am I freckly?

00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:45.470
[gasps] A little!

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.636
Right away, I was obsessed

00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:48.036
with how the freckles came out.

00:00:48.036 --> 00:00:50.210
It's a strange and kind of messy process,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.292
but they do end up looking

00:00:51.292 --> 00:00:53.210
really natural and cute.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.480
But I highly recommend you do this topless

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.988
or with a paper towel
stuffed into your shirt.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.977
I wanted to try the
Milani Conceal + Perfect

00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:05.250
Smooth Finish Cream-To-Powder Foundation

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.210
because I saw people
saying this was a dupe

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.181
for the KVD Good Apple Balm.

00:01:09.181 --> 00:01:11.730
It's not. That foundation
is literally a balm,

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.730
so it's very slippy

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.310
and almost a little oily.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.460
This Milani one is very
thick and kind of dry.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.600
I don't like the texture of this at all.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.110
I do feel like this did a great job

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:22.185
of covering everything up,

00:01:22.185 --> 00:01:23.793
because it is full coverage,

00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:26.780
but it definitely emphasized
a lot of my texture,

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.803
and I don't love how it sat on my skin.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.910
This is the ColourPop Feather
Effect Styling Brow Wax.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:33.980
I got both the clear

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.372
and the tinted versions.

00:01:35.372 --> 00:01:38.450
Also, please excuse my
purple, stained fingers.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.460
This product is...a little strange.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.101
I do think that it gives your brows

00:01:43.101 --> 00:01:44.480
that fluffy, feathered look,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.614
but I had to keep dipping in over and over

00:01:46.614 --> 00:01:48.790
to get it to look the way I wanted it to.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.090
The texture of this is just very odd.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.710
Like, I had to keep checking my brush

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.241
to make sure that there
was anything even on it.

00:01:55.241 --> 00:01:56.170
If you're looking to this

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.050
as a dupe for the ABH Brow Freeze,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.620
I don't think this is one.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.720
The Brow Freeze has a way softer texture

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.770
and literally does freeze your brows.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.424
Like, they will not move.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.950
This one has way less hold,

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.780
and it doesn't feel like it dries down.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.540
Also, I feel like there's zero difference

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.553
in color between the tinted and the clear.

00:02:12.553 --> 00:02:13.790
So weird.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.330
Now let's talk about
the blush of my dreams!

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.030
The Melt Cosmetics Cream Blushlight.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:20.863
You guys,

00:02:20.863 --> 00:02:22.220
I didn't know how this was going to go

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.710
because I had already
powdered my entire face,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:25.830
but I took a risk

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.450
and I just applied the blush on top,

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.900
and oh, my God.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.584
This blush is so gorgeous,

00:02:30.584 --> 00:02:32.160
and it didn't mess up the foundation

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.002
or powder underneath at all.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.520
I'm in love right now.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.480
And because I'm obviously
a huge blush lover,

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.763
I had to apply more and more and more,

00:02:46.763 --> 00:02:47.836
and it layered beautifully.

00:02:47.836 --> 00:02:49.250
It's totally buildable.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.628
I fully understand now

00:02:50.628 --> 00:02:52.954
why this has been sold out everywhere!

00:02:57.138 --> 00:02:58.410
That's good.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.826
These are the Danessa
Myricks Beauty Colorfix

00:03:00.826 --> 00:03:02.740
Eye, Cheek &amp; Lip Cream Pigments.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.470
These are multiuse pigments, and they come

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.848
in a bunch of different
colors and finishes.

00:03:06.848 --> 00:03:09.660
Danessa Myricks, who is a
wonderful makeup artist,

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.220
always uses these on her models

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.220
to create, like, the most beautiful looks,

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.010
so I was dying to try them.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.280
These pigments are no joke.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.890
Literally one drop is all you need.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.160
I definitely used too
much, but I'm so impressed

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.950
not only by how pigmented they are,

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.903
but how many ways you can use them.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:26.540
I used them for under-eye corrector,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.890
blush, eyeliner, and lipstick.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.815
Once these dry down,

00:03:29.815 --> 00:03:31.490
they're definitely staying put.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.730
This was not my best makeup work,

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.013
but I was just having a good time

00:03:35.013 --> 00:03:36.763
playing around with these.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.722
Minimal, skinlike makeup is
kind of like the norm now,

00:03:40.722 --> 00:03:43.200
and this Fenty Beauty Eaze
Drop Blurring Skin Tint

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.040
totally makes sense for the time.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.573
It's actually way less liquidy

00:03:46.573 --> 00:03:48.014
than I imagined it to be.

00:03:48.014 --> 00:03:50.764
And, as expected, the
coverage was pretty minimal,

00:03:50.764 --> 00:03:52.300
but this skin tint is super buildable,

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.640
so I just added more where
I felt like I needed it.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.120
Highly recommend using a brush

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.200
if you want to get the
most coverage out of it.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.350
The finish is pretty nice,
and it does dry down,

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.730
so you don't have to
worry about any tackiness.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.680
I am just so not a
skin-tint kind of person,

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.740
but this one gives you that

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:07.930
your-skin-but-better look

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.080
that I think a lot of
people would be into.

